[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: ngspice Corpus Compatibility Track

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-CORPUS-004
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded transient endpoint representation alignment
STATEMENT: >>>
For finite nonnegative transient coordinates outside a named reference table, the corpus comparator shall align to the nearest endpoint only when the coordinate differs by at most four adjacent representable double values. Larger excursions shall fail rather than extrapolate. Interior points shall retain linear interpolation. AC matching shall retain its separately declared policy. The changed comparison policy shall identify a distinct burndown series.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: CorpusPolicy.Reference and CorpusReport.ComparisonPolicy v2. Verification: CorpusContracts.TransientEndpointAllowsOnlyBoundedBinaryRepresentationDifference checks both endpoints, four/five ULP boundary, malformed coordinates and interior interpolation. Original tests/resistance/res_simple.cir exposes 6.000000000000001e-9 versus printed 6.000000e-9. Evidence: evidence/corpus-common-causes.json. This is finite axis alignment, not a global waveform error bound or permission for arbitrary extrapolation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-033
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded scalar time and frequency decorations
STATEMENT: >>>
The shared bounded scalar parser shall accept a single optional case-insensitive s or Hz decoration following a finite number and an existing supported engineering scale. Decorations shall not alter the scale: MS is milli with s decoration and MEGHz is mega with Hz decoration. Unknown tails, expressions, malformed exponents and nonfinite scaled results shall remain explicit errors. This profile shall not claim dimensional unit checking or ngspice's general trailing-letter or expression grammar.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: quantity::spice_scalar. Verification: tests/scalar_decorations.rs analytical cases, negative cases and 512 seeded Proptest cases (0x5350494345535546); full regression and corpus first-blocker comparison in evidence/corpus-common-causes.json. Reference: ngspice user manual, sections on scale factors and letters following a number, https://ngspice.sourceforge.io/docs/ngspice-manual.pdf . Standard Rust number parsing and existing scale factors are reused; no new dependency or expression parser.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-CORPUS-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Shared bounded importer command
STATEMENT: >>>
The --import-ngspice CLI operation shall call the existing library importer over at most 1 MiB of UTF-8 stdin and return its typed request or structured error. Import shall not simulate or execute control commands. It shall not introduce another parser or silently broaden unsupported syntax.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/main.rs CLI adapter and netlist::import_ngspice_request. Verification: tests/import_cli.rs successful typed translation and structured control-block rejection; existing malformed/property importer checks. Evidence: evidence/corpus-matrix-verification.json. CLI and library share lowering; this does not imply broad dialect conformance.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-CORPUS-002
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Exhaustive accounted corpus outcomes
STATEMENT: >>>
The comparison campaign shall prepopulate every discovered candidate deck row and retain its path, source scope, exact available hash and observed importer diagnostics. Default inventory shall use upstream Git-tracked circuit extensions including .deck and bounded extensionless .end decks; explicit filesystem mode shall be available. Rejected, unsupported, linked/missing, partial, failed and budget-unfinished work shall never be reported as compared passes. Accepted declarative requests shall compare named node voltages on both LU and faer against bounded ngspice output, retaining declared observation-only edits, units, tolerances, sampled coordinates and raw logs. Additional declared analyses not compared by the one-analysis importer shall remain partial. Feature hints shall be distinguished from isolated root causes.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: CorpusCommand, CorpusRunner and CorpusPolicy in dotnet/Simulator.Benchmarks; existing bounded ProcessRunner and Tables. Verification: CorpusContracts inventory/resource/outcome/axis/observation negative and FsCheck properties, actual tracked upstream scan and local synthetic pass/rejection/failure cases. All node voltages and at most 200 representative coordinates per signal are the finite comparison basis; no branch-current or global waveform bound. External control/library execution is excluded. Evidence: evidence/corpus-matrix-verification.json and the retained matrix. No copied upstream deck bodies are redistributed in Git.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-CORPUS-003
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Per-run results issue and honest burndown
STATEMENT: >>>
Each finalized corpus invocation shall default to creating one GitHub results issue in the explicitly identified origin repository, with outcome counts, diagnostic/feature triage checklists and burndown observations. Explicit offline mode shall record no publication. Publishing failure shall remain distinct from numerical results and shall not be called uploaded. A standalone SVG and numeric history shall update automatically. Remaining work shall include every nonpassing outcome; histories shall only share a series when deck hashes, inventory mode, comparison policy/tolerances and oracle executable match. A first run shall be a baseline, not fabricated progress. Partial checkpoints shall preserve valid prior evidence without claiming guaranteed recovery or publication after forced termination.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: CorpusPresentation, CorpusCommand publishing/finalization and scripts/Run-CorpusComparison.ps1. The maintained authenticated gh CLI receives complete noninteractive arguments and a body file; no source push or CI dispatch is implied. Source, input and executable provenance is retained; issue URL is verified and publisher diagnostics retained. Verification: CorpusContracts chart/history/target tests, actual issue creation, structured local output and XML-valid SVG; scoped coverage and mutation outcomes in evidence/corpus-matrix-verification.json. Permanent filesystem/network failure and arbitrary OS process containment remain unqualified.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-032
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Independent AC bias and excitation
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded AC importer shall retain independent-source DC values for nonlinear bias, lower explicit AC magnitudes and phases separately, and assign zero small-signal excitation to sources without an AC clause. The raw typed API's nominal-amplitude convention shall remain unchanged.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/netlist.rs::import_ngspice_request. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs DC/AC separation and zero-excitation cases; tests/model_charge.rs independent nonlinear-bias transfer; evidence/named-ac-qualification-diode-constant-charge.json external comparison. Derived requirement remains Draft.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MODEL-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-030
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit constant-charge diode model lowering
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded importer shall accept positive CJO/CJ0 only with explicit M=0, map it to the diode_with_capacitance profile, accept explicitly zero RS/TT, and reject nonzero grading/series/transport, unknown parameters and duplicate canonical parameter names. CJO=0 with M=0 shall map to a known zero-charge legacy diode. Basic D lines may add one positive farad value after the explicit thermal voltage.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/netlist.rs typed bounded diode model parameters and basic parser. Verification: tests/model_charge.rs supported compact/mixed-case/alias forms, temperature/ideality units, required M=0, zero-charge mapping and malformed/unsupported parameter cases. Geometry and general depletion charge remain unsupported.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MODEL-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-031
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Raw deck byte bound before normalization
STATEMENT: >>>
Both bounded ngspice parsing entry points shall reject raw text above 1 MiB before allocating logical-line/model normalization structures. Comments and unsupported records shall not bypass the input byte budget.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/netlist.rs::parse_ngspice_basic and import_ngspice_request. Verification: tests/model_charge.rs oversized comment deck; existing generated parser diagnostics remain applicable.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: NGC-030

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-001
TITLE: Full corpus inventory
STATEMENT: >>>
The project shall inventory every recognized circuit fixture in a user-provided ngspice checkout without modifying that checkout, recording path, content hash, lexical feature markers and an explicit compatibility status.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/Inventory-Ngspice.cs. Initial observed baseline: 118 test circuit files at local revision e8285746c.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-002
TITLE: No implied full compatibility
STATEMENT: >>>
Each ngspice corpus fixture shall be classified as candidate_basic, supported, unsupported or future_feature. A fixture may be marked supported only after it executes against a documented result oracle.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The corpus is a roadmap and regression source, not a blanket behavioral compatibility claim.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-003
TITLE: External corpus integrity
STATEMENT: >>>
Compatibility tooling shall treat the ngspice checkout as read-only and shall retain source attribution and license context for copied fixtures or result oracles.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The current checkout reports a mixed license context with Modified BSD as the general test/example baseline; inspect upstream COPYING before copying any additional material.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-004
TITLE: One hundred-family compatibility campaign
STATEMENT: >>>
The project shall maintain a stable, machine-readable campaign of exactly one hundred named ngspice compatibility feature families. Each family shall have an explicit status selected from supported, import_only, supported_api_only, planned, future or unsupported. A status shall not imply compatibility beyond its stated scope.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/Plan-NgspiceFeatureFamilies.cs. The list deliberately separates deck import, public typed API capability, planned work and permanently unsupported interactive/plugin mechanisms.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-005
TITLE: Independent executable oracle
STATEMENT: >>>
When a curated fixture is promoted to supported, verification shall compare a documented observable against an independently executed ngspice batch result or another documented analytic oracle. The verifier shall preserve the command, executable identity, fixture hash and tolerance as evidence.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/Run-NgspiceOracle.cs creates a fixture-hash-named build directory and emits executable path, fixture hash, exit code and complete batch log. scripts/Compare-NgspiceOracle.cs compares the named i(V1) observable for the curated res_simple fixture at a 1e-12 tolerance. This prevents importer acceptance from being mistaken for numerical compatibility.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-006
TITLE: Safe compact DC-source import
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded ngspice importer shall normalize DC <value> and DC=<value> source forms and inline semicolon comments. It shall reject source waveform or AC tails that it cannot represent, rather than silently reducing them to DC values.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/netlist.rs parse_ngspice_basic. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs compact form and waveform rejection tests.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-007
TITLE: Pulse waveform semantics
STATEMENT: >>>
The typed transient API shall represent a bounded periodic pulse waveform with finite levels, nonnegative delay/rise/fall/width, a positive period and no pulse phase duration exceeding that period.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/waveform.rs Waveform::Pulse. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs exact plateau/edge and invalid-period tests.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-008
TITLE: Bounded transient-deck lowering
STATEMENT: >>>
The ngspice importer shall lower exactly one two-value .tran directive into a typed configured transient request. Optional transient fields outside that profile shall fail explicitly rather than being discarded.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/netlist.rs import_ngspice_request. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs transient lowering test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-009
TITLE: Evidence-backed campaign reviews
STATEMENT: >>>
The items 2 through 5 implementation campaign shall expose one hundred numbered points and self-review gates at points 50 and 100 in a local web page. Review entries shall identify their evidence and shall not represent fictional people or activity as real review participants.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: docs/campaign-2-to-5.html.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-010
TITLE: Whole-checkout corpus inventory
STATEMENT: >>>
The ngspice inventory shall enumerate recognized netlists across the supplied checkout, record the top-level source scope as tests, examples or other, and never modify that checkout.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/Inventory-Ngspice.cs. This distinguishes regression fixtures from illustrative and auxiliary source material before compatibility promotion.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-011
TITLE: Selected-fixture dependency manifest
STATEMENT: >>>
The compatibility project shall maintain a checked-in manifest of selected external fixtures, their upstream path and revision, promotion state, and exact missing feature dependencies. A fixture shall not be marked oracle-passing while a listed dependency remains unmet.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: compat/ngspice/selected-fixtures.json.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-012
TITLE: VCCS controlled-source polarity
STATEMENT: >>>
The typed circuit API and bounded ngspice importer shall support a voltage-controlled current source whose p-to-n current equals transconductance times the control positive-minus-negative voltage. Control terminals shall be distinct valid nodes and gain shall be finite.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: circuit::Element::Vccs, compile::compile and netlist::parse_ngspice_basic. Verification: tests/controlled_sources.rs and tests/ngspice_compat.rs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-013
TITLE: VCVS controlled-source polarity
STATEMENT: >>>
The typed circuit API and bounded ngspice importer shall support a voltage-controlled voltage source whose output positive-minus-negative voltage equals gain times the control positive-minus-negative voltage. The source shall use an explicit MNA branch unknown and reject invalid control terminals or nonfinite gain.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: circuit::Element::Vcvs, compile::compile and netlist::parse_ngspice_basic. Verification: tests/controlled_sources.rs and tests/ngspice_compat.rs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-014
TITLE: CCCS controlled-current compatibility
STATEMENT: >>>
The typed circuit API and bounded ngspice importer shall support an F current-controlled current source whose p-to-n current equals gain times the p-to-n MNA branch current of a named voltage-defined control element. The control identifier shall be nonempty, the gain finite, and an absent or non-branch control identifier shall fail compilation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: circuit::Element::Cccs, compile::compile and netlist::parse. Verification: tests/controlled_sources.rs and tests/ngspice_compat.rs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-015
TITLE: CCVS controlled-voltage compatibility
STATEMENT: >>>
The typed circuit API and bounded ngspice importer shall support an H current-controlled voltage source whose output p-minus-n voltage equals transresistance times the p-to-n MNA branch current of a named voltage-defined control element. The source shall use its own explicit MNA branch unknown, reject invalid control identifiers during compilation, and retain transresistance as a finite scalar in ohms.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: circuit::Element::Ccvs, compile::compile and netlist::parse. Verification: tests/controlled_sources.rs and tests/ngspice_compat.rs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-016
TITLE: Bounded exponential source compatibility
STATEMENT: >>>
The typed transient API and bounded deck importer shall support compact and whitespace-delimited six-parameter SPICE EXP sources with an initial level, pulsed level, rise delay and time constant, then fall delay and time constant. All values shall be finite, delays shall be ordered and nonnegative, time constants shall be positive, and the source shall publish both transition delays as solver breakpoints.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: waveform::Waveform::Exponential and netlist::import_ngspice_request. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-017
TITLE: Bounded continuation-record lowering
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded ngspice importer shall fold an explicit plus-prefixed continuation record into its immediately preceding logical record before tokenization. It shall reject orphan or empty continuation records rather than inferring a target record. Inline comments and full-line comments shall remain excluded from the folded input.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: netlist::parse_ngspice_basic. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-018
TITLE: Executable fixture-manifest integrity
STATEMENT: >>>
The selected ngspice fixture manifest shall have an executable validator that rejects duplicate, absolute, traversal, or out-of-scope source paths; missing canonical upstream SHA-256 hashes; unknown promotion states; missing source attribution; malformed or duplicate required-feature names; and any oracle-passing fixture that still declares missing features.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/Validate-NgspiceFixtureManifest.cs. Verification: its successful execution over compat/ngspice/selected-fixtures.json and negative malformed manifests in the development workflow.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-019
TITLE: Bounded output-directive import validation
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded ngspice importer shall classify .print and .plot as import-only directives only when they declare a supported analysis name and at least one output expression, and shall classify .probe as import-only only when it has at least one expression. Malformed output directives shall fail instead of being silently discarded.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: netlist::parse_ngspice_basic. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-020
TITLE: Complex AC source phasors
STATEMENT: >>>
The typed AC request shall accept bounded, unique, finite complex phasors for independent voltage and current sources. A phasor shall replace its source's nominal real small-signal excitation without changing the DC circuit. The ngspice importer shall lower AC amplitude and optional phase in degrees into those phasors and shall preserve p-to-n source polarity.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: api::AcSourcePhasor, ac::ac_with_source_phasors and netlist::import_ngspice_request. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs, tests/analyses.rs and tests/providers.rs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-021
TITLE: Bounded delayed and damped sine sources
STATEMENT: >>>
The typed transient API and bounded deck importer shall support three-value, five-value, and six-value SPICE SIN parameter lists. Five and six value forms shall represent finite offset, amplitude, positive frequency, nonnegative delay and damping, and an optional phase in degrees; evaluation shall hold the offset before delay and publish the delay as a solver breakpoint.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: waveform::Waveform::DampedSine and netlist::bounded_sine. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-022
TITLE: Ground-alias normalization
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded netlist parsers shall normalize the case-insensitive labels gnd and ground to the mandatory numeric reference node 0 before node identity creation. The aliases shall not create separate nodes or alter the p-to-n sign conventions.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: netlist::parse. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-023
TITLE: AC-qualified reactive component import
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded AC deck importer shall accept a trailing ac=<value> qualifier on resistor, capacitor, and inductor cards. The qualifier shall replace the component scalar only in the lowered AC request; the source deck's DC scalar and the typed circuit's DC semantics shall otherwise remain unchanged.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: netlist::import_ngspice_request. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-024
TITLE: Bounded named diode-model import
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded ngspice importer shall lower a named .model <name> D card with positive finite IS and N parameters into the typed Shockley diode saturation current and 300 K nominal thermal voltage scaled by N. Unknown model names, duplicate model names, non-diode model kinds, unsupported parameters, and invalid values shall fail explicitly.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: netlist::bounded_diode_models. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-025
TITLE: Bounded diode temperature import
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded ngspice importer shall accept at most one one-value .temp directive in Celsius. The value shall be converted to a positive Kelvin temperature and used with the Boltzmann-over-charge constant to calculate the nominal diode thermal voltage before ideality scaling. Invalid or repeated temperature directives shall fail explicitly.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: netlist::bounded_temperature. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-026
TITLE: Bounded options-card import
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded ngspice importer shall accept only the output/reporting option names LIST, NODE, POST, TRANS and noacct, which do not change typed-circuit numerical semantics. Unsupported options shall fail explicitly rather than being silently discarded.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: netlist::parse_ngspice_basic. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-027
TITLE: Stable netlist identifier case normalization
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded netlist parser shall normalize node labels to lowercase and element identifiers to uppercase. The normalization shall be case-insensitive at input and stable in the public typed circuit, so cross-reference identifiers such as current-controlled source controls are reproducible.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: netlist::parse. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-028
TITLE: Reproducible bounded deck lowering
STATEMENT: >>>
For identical bounded ngspice deck text and case identifier, repeated import shall produce byte-identical serialized typed requests and the same request provenance hash. The guarantee applies to supported bounded lowering only and does not claim cross-platform floating-point bitwise reproducibility.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: netlist::import_ngspice_request and provenance::request_hash. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-029
TITLE: Bounded AC source auxiliary-tail import
STATEMENT: >>>
For a deck that requests only a bounded .ac analysis, the importer shall accept a voltage or current source with DC, AC, five-value SIN, DISTOF1 and DISTOF2 clauses only in the fully validated ordering DC value, AC magnitude, SIN five finite values, DISTOF1 finite value and DISTOF2 finite value. It shall lower the AC magnitude to the typed phasor and shall not claim transient or distortion analysis support from the ignored auxiliary clauses. Any other source tail remains unsupported.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: netlist::import_ngspice_request. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs::ngspice_lowpass_fixture_lowers_to_the_declared_ac_response and scripts/Compare-NgspiceLowpassOracle.cs. The oracle uses a 5e-8 bound because ngspice's human-readable .print table rounds this fixture's two complex components; it is not a general solver-accuracy target.
<<<
